===================================

Running emberx without a build, after PR #73 (ember-source 7) is merged. Today `npm test` builds first only
because the browser suite needs dist/: @memserver/model, in node_modules, imports @emberx/string, and that
resolves through the package's exports to dist/. The node, Deno and doctest suites and the dev server already
bundle from packages/@emberx/*/src. In order:

1. No build for development (small PR, right after #73):
   - Until @memoria/* replaces @memserver/*, add emberxWorkspacePlugin to the esbuild plugin qunitx loads
     (package.json#qunitx.plugins), so the browser suite resolves @emberx/* to sources too.
   - Then drop the build from `npm test`, point check-benchmarks.ts at sources, and delete `build:dev` and
     `make build-dev`. The one build left (build.ts) is for publishing: test-release, Docker, CI's package job.
   - CI runs the test jobs with no build step, so a dependency that needs dist/ again fails CI at once.
2. @memoria/* replaces @memserver/* (its own PR): if @memoria/* imports no @emberx/* package, delete the
   step 1 bridge; the CI guard from step 1 confirms it.
3. TypeScript that node runs by stripping types (small PR, any time): constructor parameter properties
   (`constructor(private limit)`) become plain fields, type-only imports use `import type`, and tsconfig turns
   on erasableSyntaxOnly and verbatimModuleSyntax so typecheck rejects what node cannot run. Then
   `node packages/@emberx/string/src/...` runs as it is.
4. Any source file under `deno run` (small PR, after #73): a root deno.json with experimentalDecorators and an
   import map from @emberx/* to packages/@emberx/*/src/index.ts, and from @ember/* and @glimmer/* to their
   files in ember-source, whose own exports only have ember-source/@ember/... paths.
5. The same under node (small PR, after 4): scripts/register.ts with module.registerHooks, resolving the same
   names and compiling decorators with esbuild: `node --import ./scripts/register.ts any-file.ts`.
6. No compile step at all (long term, not ours alone): once JS engines ship standard decorators and emberx moves
   @tracked, @action and @service off legacy decorators, step 5 only resolves names. Browsers always need .ts
   compiled, which qunitx and the dev server already do in memory, with no dist/.

Fewer scripts, as in qunitx (scripts/ there: check-benchmarks.ts, check-coverage.ts, release-consumer-test.ts,
sync-jsr-version.ts, test-release.sh). Each script is one more file a newcomer has to read, so a bare command
replaces it wherever one can:
- Same as qunitx, kept: check-benchmarks.ts, release-consumer-test.ts, test-release.sh.
- scripts/clean.ts: done, now `rm -rf` in package.json, as qunitx's build:cold.
- test-node.ts, test-deno.ts and lib/test-bundle.js: bundle the suites with esbuild first only because the
  sources do not run as they are. After steps 4 and 5 above they become `node --import ./scripts/register.ts
  --test test/node.ts` and `deno test test/node.ts`, as qunitx's `node --test test/index.ts`, with
  test/setup-dom.js imported by test/node.ts itself.
- test-doctests.ts: after step 4, `deno test --doc README.md packages/@emberx/*/README.md packages/@emberx/*/src`,
  as qunitx's test:doctests. The `// => value` comments become explicit assertions, which `deno test --doc`
  does not add for us.
- dev.ts: no qunitx counterpart (qunitx has no app to serve). Keep it, but let esbuild serve it (its serve API
  with `fallback` for the blog's URLs) instead of the hand-written node:http server.
- release.ts: kept. `npm version --workspaces --include-workspace-root` bumps all seven package.json files but
  leaves the exact @emberx/* dependency pins at the old version (checked with npm 11.19), and the packages must
  be published leaf-first.
- After all of the above, scripts/ is check-benchmarks.ts, dev.ts, register.ts, release.ts,
  release-consumer-test.ts and test-release.sh, plus lib/chrome-bench.js and lib/esbuild-plugins.js.
